Warning [jet.UnusedParameter]: Parameter `h` is never used.
  --> tests/ui_lint/shared_loop.jet:1:10
    |
  1 | noop: fn(h: Shared<Int>) { print(0) }
    |          ^
 Why: An unused parameter often means the function contract or implementation is incomplete; Jet keeps this warning-only so prototypes stay unblocked.
 Fix: Use `h`, rename it to `_h` when it is intentionally unused, or remove it from the function contract.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/L0102

Warning [jet.SharedAutoClone]: Auto-cloned `h` inside a loop; consider hoisting or caching
  --> tests/ui_lint/shared_loop.jet:4:18
    |
  4 |     loop -> noop(h)
    |                  ^
 Why: Shared handles are cloned when used across a loop boundary
 Fix: Hoist `h` before the loop, or clone once outside
More: jet-lang.dev/e/L0202

Warning [jet.InferredNeverReturn]: Public function `loop_user` always diverges but does not declare `Never`
  --> tests/ui_lint/shared_loop.jet:3:1
    |
  3 | loop_user: fn(h: Shared<Int>) {
    | ^^^^^^^^^
 Why: Inferred divergence is useful to callers but is not part of the written API contract
 Fix: Write `-> Never` as the return type, for example `loop_user: fn() -> Never`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/L2421
